It is understood and agreed that these policies are primary and not contributory.  It shall be
an affirmative obligation upon Contractor to immediately notify in writing the District risk manager,
the City risk manager, City Clerk, and City Attorney of any fact, circumstances, or occurrence that
has resulted in or may result in the cancellation or substantive change of any insurance coverage
required by this Contract, and failure to do so shall be construed to be a breach of this Contract.
The City and the District shall be named as additional insureds/loss payees on CFD’s
insurance policies, except Workers’ Compensation, and CFD shall provide upon request by the City
or the District copies of endorsements providing this coverage.  The failure of the City or the District
to request or review such policies, endorsements, or certificates shall not affect the City’s rights, the
District’s rights, or CFD’s obligations hereunder.
The City and the District, individually or collectively, have the right to reject a certificate of
insurance if any insurance company engaged by CFD to provide the insurance coverages required
by this Contract is widely regarded in the insurance industry as financially unstable.  Any insurance
company providing coverage under this Contract shall have a minimum A.M. Best rating of A-
(Excellent).
CFD will pay the District employees’ salaries and Workers’ Compensation premiums due
under this Contract as temporary employees of CFD.
8.
General Provisions.
A.
Amendments.  Any changes, modifications, revisions or amendments to this Contract
