### Page 3 of 4

```text
Contract between City of Cheyenne and Cheyenne Frontier Days, Inc.
3
which are mutually agreed upon by the parties to this Contract shall be incorporated by written
instrument, executed and signed by all parties to this Contract.
B.
Applicable Law.  The construction, interpretation and enforcement of this Contract
shall be governed by the laws of the State of Wyoming.  The courts of the State of  Wyoming shall
have jurisdiction over this Contract and the parties, and the venue shall be in the First Judicial
District Court, Laramie County, Wyoming.
C.
Compliance with Laws.  CFD shall keep informed of and comply with all applicable
federal, state and local laws and regulations in the performance of this Contract.

D.
Entirety of Contract.  This Contract, consisting of four pages, and Attachment A,
consisting of four pages, represent the entire and integrated Contract between the parties and
supersedes all prior negotiations, representations and agreements, whether written or oral.
E.
Indemnification.  CFD agrees to indemnify, hold harmless and defend the City and
the District from and against any and all liabilities, claims, penalties, forfeitures and suits, and the
cost and expenses incident thereto including reasonable attorney’s fees, which may hereafter arise
as a result of death or bodily injury to any person, destruction or damage to any property,
contamination of or adverse effects on the environment, or any violation of governmental laws,
regulations or orders to the extent caused by (1) CFD’s breach of any term or provision of this
Contract, or (2) any negligent or wrongful act, error or omission by CFD or its employees or
subcontractors in the performance of this Contract. CFD acknowledges that it may incur a financial
obligation to the City or the District pursuant to the terms of this paragraph.
F.
Independent Contractor.  CFD shall function as an independent contractor for the
purposes of this Contract.  CFD shall assume sole responsibility for any debts or liabilities that may
be incurred by CFD in fulfilling the terms of this Contract.  Nothing in this Contract shall be
interpreted as authorizing CFD, or its agents or employees, to act as an agent or representative of the
City or the District or to incur any obligation of any kind on the behalf of the City or the District.
G.
Notice.  All notices arising out of or from the provisions of this Contract shall be in
writing and given to the parties either by regular mail or delivery in person at the addresses indicated
above.
H.
Nondiscrimination.  CFD shall comply with the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the
Wyoming Fair Employment Practices Act, Wyo. Stat. § 27-9-105 et seq., and the Americans with
Disabilities Act (ADA), 42 U.S.C. § 12101, et seq.
I.
Prior Approval.  This Contract shall not be binding upon either party and  no services
shall be performed under the terms of this Contract and no payment shall be  made until this Contract
has been reduced to writing and approved by all necessary authorities.
```

